<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged with the Info.plist the Tauri CLI generates, so this file carries only the
  keys Tauri does not know about. Deliberately nothing else: overwriting a value
  Tauri computes — the version, the bundle identifier — introduces conflicts that
  show up as a bundle that will not launch.

  A usage description is not a formality. Without NSMicrophoneUsageDescription the
  process is terminated the moment it touches the microphone: no exception, no log
  line, and for a tray app with no window, nothing at all on screen. The app simply
  disappears.

  The strings are user-visible — they are the entire text of the system dialog, and
  the only chance to say why before someone decides. Written for that person, not to
  satisfy a linter.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Magi records only while you hold its hotkey, and transcribes what you said on this Mac. No audio ever leaves your computer.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
